1491	///   through `pre_replacement_damage_gate` (0-damage / protection / prohibition
1492	///   gates) WITHOUT applying any damage yet.
1493	/// - **Phase B (Batch replace):** pass the whole proposed-event slice through
1494	///   `replace_combat_damage_batch`, which runs the replacement pipeline per
1495	///   event but aggregates each `Prevention::All` shield's prevented amount.
1496	/// - **Phase C (Apply + bookkeeping):** apply each surviving post-replacement
1497	///   event via `apply_damage_after_replacement`, then run the player-batching
1498	///   and commander-damage bookkeeping. Afterward, fire each prevention shield's
1499	///   `runtime_execute` rider exactly once against the aggregate prevented
1500	///   amount (CR 615.5 + CR 615.13).
1501	///
1502	/// Used by both the automatic assignment path and the interactive
1503	/// `AssignCombatDamage` handler.
1504	/// CR 510.2: the outcome of applying one simultaneous combat-damage batch.
1505	///
1506	/// An enum rather than a `Vec<GameEvent>` plus an out-param: the previous return
1507	/// type had no channel for a pause, which is exactly why the pause was silently
1508	/// discarded. A caller now cannot ignore it without a compile error.
1509	pub(crate) enum CombatDamageBatch {
1510	    /// Every assignment applied, every lifelink gain completed, and Phase D fired.
1511	    Complete(Vec<GameEvent>),
1512	    /// CR 616.1: a lifelink life-gain event met two or more co-applicable
1513	    /// replacement effects and the gaining player must choose which applies
1514	    /// first. All damage is already dealt. The unfinished tail is parked in
1515	    /// `state.pending_combat_lifelink`; `state.pending_replacement` holds the
1516	    /// paused source's own `LifeGain` and is the resume's authority.
1517	    Paused {
1518	        events: Vec<GameEvent>,
1519	        /// Boxed: `WaitingFor` is ~1720 bytes against `Complete`'s 24, so an
1520	        /// inline field would make every `Complete` return pay the pause's size
1521	        /// (`clippy::large_enum_variant`).
1522	        waiting_for: Box<WaitingFor>,
1523	    },
1524	}
